; case: stack-allocation
; verdict: reject
; ambiguous: yes
; tests: externality=pass implementation-independence=pass non-prescription=fail
; failing-test: non-prescription
; rationale: AMBIGUOUS, resolved REJECT. A stack size looks like a resource requirement, and
;   `rt-static-up-v1` really does require "separate statically allocated task stacks". But the
;   REQUIREMENT is that each task has its own bounded stack; the NUMBER is an allocation. §7.3
;   assigns concrete allocations to the engine, and §7.6 checks the result against the actual
;   linked sections — so a number written here is either redundant with what the engine derives
;   or in conflict with it, and a conflict between a description and a linked image is resolved
;   by the image. Test 3 settles it: the field prescribes a layout decision rather than stating
;   a guarantee. What eADL may state is the bounded-stack requirement and the guard behavior.
; other-side: belongs in the engine: the derived allocation, checked against the linked image,
;   with the stack bound's evidence category recorded separately
;
(defsystem app.rt
  (task sensor
    (period 10 ms)
    (deadline 10 ms)
    (priority 1)
    (stack-allocation 4 KiB)))
